# Consumer-Grade Mobile App UI Overhaul

You are completely right. A simple responsive "squished desktop" design is not good enough if the team is using this software like a native mobile app (like Zomato or Amazon) on the field. They need a true mobile-first, app-like experience. 

I will completely restructure the mobile view to mimic a modern consumer mobile app.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Bottom Tab Navigation (Native App Feel)
- **Remove the Hamburger Sidebar** completely for mobile users.
- Introduce a **Bottom Navigation Bar** that stays fixed to the bottom of the screen.
- Tabs will include: **Home (Dashboard)**, **Leads**, **Events**, **Tasks**, and a **Menu** tab (to open a full-screen drawer for settings/finance/inventory).
- This is exactly how apps like Zomato, Instagram, and Amazon structure their primary navigation.

### 2. Sleek Mobile App Header
- The top bar will be minimized on mobile. It will just show the Page Title centered, and your profile picture/notification icon. 

### 3. Data Tables ➝ Mobile Cards
Desktop-style tables with horizontal scrolling are terrible on mobile. I will convert the major data views into **beautiful mobile cards** (similar to how an Amazon order list or Zomato restaurant list looks).

- **For the Major Screens (`Leads`, `Events`, `Tasks`):** I will rewrite the code so that on mobile, it renders a modern, tappable card layout instead of a table. 
  - E.g., A Lead card will show the person's name in bold, an avatar, their status badge, and budget, perfectly spaced.
- **For the Rest of the App:** I will add a global CSS engine that automatically transforms all remaining desktop tables into stacked vertical cards on mobile screens to ensure zero horizontal scrolling anywhere.

### 4. Spacing and Touch Targets
- Increase padding on buttons and list items to ensure they are easy to tap with a thumb.
- Remove unnecessary box-shadows and borders to give a clean, edge-to-edge iOS/Android native app look.

